    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Tai kingdom founded around 1238 when local chiefs expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> governor of Sukhothai.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ram-khamhaeng">Ram Khamhaeng</a> in the late thirteenth century its overlordship stretched across much of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> made it a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> in 1378 and absorbed it around 1438, but it became the founding kingdom of Thai history.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ram-khamhaeng">Ram Khamhaeng</a>'s inscription says a bell hung at the palace gate so that any subject with a grievance could ring it and be heard by the king.</p></aside>
    </section>

